From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 04:46:40 +0000
Subject: clk: qcom: gcc-ipq8074: enable parents while switching nss_crypto_clk_src

An RCG whose root is enabled does not switch to a source that is not
running. The NSS crypto PLL has no other consumer and is off at boot,
so when the bootloader leaves the crypto RCG root enabled,
assigned-clock-rates on the PPE node switches it to the stopped PLL and
the update times out:

  nss_crypto_clk_src: rcg didn't update its configuration.

Set CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE so the clock core runs the parents across the
switch, as gcc-sc7180 does for gcc_sdcc2_apps_clk_src.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq8074.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-ipq8074.c
@@ -1198,6 +1198,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 nss_crypto_clk_sr
 		.name = "nss_crypto_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = gcc_xo_nss_crypto_pll_gpll0,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(gcc_xo_nss_crypto_pll_gpll0),
+		.flags = CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE,
 		.ops = &clk_rcg2_ops,
 	},
 };
